{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/claude-code-settings.json",
  "_description": "Default profile — high-stakes review and analysis mode. All mutations (Edit, Write, dev commands that change state) prompt for approval. Allow list is deliberately narrow: read-only inspection, version control reads, build/test/lint that doesn't mutate external state. Use this profile for code review, audits, Iskra fade-out triage, primus-planning analysis, or any work where forward motion should pause on every mutation. For active development, use acceptEdits. For scratch/MVP, use bypass.",
  "_safety_notes": [
    "default ≠ acceptEdits. Edit/Write are NOT auto-approved here — every file change prompts. This is intentional: the profile is for reviewing, not for shipping.",
    "Allow list contains only read-only ops, build/test/lint that produces no side effects, and git inspection. Anything that mutates filesystem, packages, infrastructure, or remote state goes through the prompt.",
    "If you find yourself approving the same prompt repeatedly, you are probably in active development — switch to acceptEdits profile.",
    "Bash(env) and friends are denied: prevents ANTHROPIC_API_KEY leakage into conversation context.",
    "Compound bash (&&, ;, ||, |, eval, bash -c, command substitution) is denied to prevent allow/deny bypass via chaining. This is the policy backbone.",
    "Self-modification of CLAUDE.md and .claude/** is denied — change those outside Claude Code. .harness/** is allowed because it is the working surface for harness automation."
  ],
